meegotouch backend: theme effects through meegofeedbackd

Qt 5 apps can't load libmeegotouch, so the backend speaks MFeedbackPlayer's protocol to
meegofeedbackd itself (/tmp/mfeedbackd/player.sock: the protocol version and the app's name,
then one effect name per playback), and maps QtFeedback's effects to the theme's names
(Press/Release: priority2_static_*, the weak ones: priority2_pannable_*, drag: grab, drop,
move, Appear/Disappear: popup, close). Qt Mobility's played priority2_static_press for all.

